{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___, one of your care team doctors. You're here today for your high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. My 25th cycle now. I’ve been doing this for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a long journey. I see you’re feeling well today—no fevers, nausea, or headaches?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel okay. Just the usual face numbness. I’ve started using a few drops of medical marijuana elixir to help with that and maybe sleep a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that noted. Any improvement so far?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not sure yet. It’s only been a few days. I’ll keep trying it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright. We’ll keep an eye on it. Today, we’ll start with IV fluids and sodium bicarbonate to protect your kidneys before the methotrexate infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, the urine alkalinization. I remember that from last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The goal is to keep your urine less acidic so the methotrexate doesn’t harm your kidneys. We’ll also restart your temozolomide today—240 mg daily for seven days on, seven off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Same as before. And leucovorin starts 24 hours after the chemo, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s correct. It helps ‘rescue’ your healthy cells from the chemo. We’ll monitor your methotrexate levels closely over the next couple of days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Last time, my sodium dropped a bit. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that in your history. You’re on desmopressin for diabetes insipidus, which can sometimes cause low sodium when combined with IV fluids. But today your sodium is 139, which is normal, so we’ll keep your desmopressin the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I don’t want to feel confused or weak again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring it. Your other labs look stable too—kidney function and liver enzymes are good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my potassium? I think it was low last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-10-13 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 3.5 this morning—slightly low but not concerning. We’ll keep an eye on it. We can supplement if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-10-13 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to start your methotrexate infusion now—19,440 mg over several hours. You’ll be closely monitored."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-10-13 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I know the drill. Let’s get it done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-10-14 05:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level came back at 0.61 last night. That’s a good sign—it’s coming down as expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-10-14 05:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right? No complications so far?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-10-14 05:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you’re doing well. Your white blood cell count is a bit low at 3.6, but that’s expected with chemo. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-10-14 05:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had any infections, so that’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-10-14 05:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll continue your leucovorin and bicarbonate. You’re also due for your next Rituxan clinic visit soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-10-14 05:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, in about a week. I’ve been getting it every three months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-10-14 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—the chemotherapy infusion was completed yesterday, and you’ve tolerated it well so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-10-14 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no side effects. I’m feeling pretty normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest methotrexate level is 0.17, which is excellent. That means it’s almost cleared from your system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re planning to discharge you today. You’ll take leucovorin and bicarbonate for one more day at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same doses as in the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly as prescribed. And continue all your regular medications—desmopressin, levetiracetam, sertraline, and the others."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling more down lately. I mentioned that to the nurse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ve scheduled you to see Dr. ___ in the psychiatry clinic. It’s important to address that, especially with everything you’re going through."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I appreciate that. And my next MRI is in a month?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, to monitor the lymphoma. So far, your treatment is on track. You’ve tolerated this cycle very well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. It’s tough, but I want to keep fighting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-10-15 00:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Make sure to call if you develop fever, confusion, or any unusual symptoms. Otherwise, follow up with your oncology team as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Everything’s ready for discharge. Your condition is stable, and you’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I’ll take care of myself and see you all next time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your discharge papers and prescriptions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll wait for her."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your methotrexate level had been higher than 0.2, we’d have kept you longer, but at 0.17, you’re safe to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I was a little nervous about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Completely understandable. But you’ve done well this round."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. One step at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And we’re here to support you every step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and rest well at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-10-15 21:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you next time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-10-13 10:16:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-10-15 21:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with recurrent primary central nervous system lymphoma was admitted for his 25th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy as part of reinduction therapy. He presented electively in stable condition and received methotrexate 8 g/m² with urinary alkalinization. Temozolomide 240 mg daily was continued on a 7-day on/7-day off cycle. Leucovorin rescue was initiated 24 hours post-infusion. Methotrexate levels declined appropriately to 0.17, and he tolerated treatment without complications. Sodium remained stable, and no adjustments were needed to desmopressin. He reported increased depressive symptoms, prompting a psychiatry clinic referral. He was discharged home with instructions to continue leucovorin and bicarbonate for 24 hours, resume all home medications, and follow up for Rituxan and MRI surveillance in one month.",
    "problems": [
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Other convulsions",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Essential and other specified forms of tremor",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Personal history of tuberculosis"
    ]
  }
}
